  "fixture": "Four distinct BAMs made deterministically by retaining 50 reference-bearing reads and respectively 1, 6, 11, 16 alternate-bearing reads at each of three loci of the bundled synthetic trio father alignment. Both callers, one DNP step and four SNP steps, plus the merged SNP plot/summary. Counts checked independently per locus and sample, exact per-sample and summary tables compared against f5b837e.",
  "runtime": "Released Linux/AMD64 0.9.9 userspace under bwrap with actual Python scientific entry point, R 4.4.2 and samtools 1.21. Each scenario shares the same four CPU affinity cores and 8192 MiB software scheduling capacity. Independent host processes use production admission, owner locks and DesktopStepScheduler. Cross-session files live on the same filesystem and the admission runtime-idle callback observes the live local engine process. No Docker daemon, GUI platform, VM mount or kernel RAM-limit timing validation.",
  "process_observation": "Scientific R and samtools descendants sampled from /proc about every 100 ms; concurrent positive CPU-tick deltas mean processes from distinct experiment trees actually received CPU during the same sampling interval. Workflow start/end timestamps separately determine concurrent SNP steps and engine lifetime overlap. Single trial per scenario.",
